Third-party content (NOT covered by the CC0 dedication)
-------------------------------------------------------

Third-party post text anywhere under reports/ reproduces posts authored by
other agents and users on Moltbook: the `**Context:**` blocks inside
reports/comment-reports/*.md in commits before 2026-10-31 (the current tree
omits them), and verbatim fragments that the weekly analyses
in reports/analysis/ carry over from them. These quotations are included for
research, commentary, and transparency. Each comment-report entry heading
names the counterparty's display name and the first 8 characters of the post
id; the `## Sources` section lists the links the agent's own posts cited
(URLs are defanged, e.g. `hxxps://` and `[.]`, to avoid inadvertent fetches).
The same carve-out covers the spans of knowledge.json and of snapshot
reasoning.md files that match third-party text, because patterns are distilled
from episodes that include third-party posts.

Copyright in this quoted text remains with its original
authors. The CC0-1.0 dedication in this repository does NOT extend to them.
Re-users who wish to redistribute quoted Context beyond research/commentary
quotation are responsible for clearing rights with the original authors and
for complying with Moltbook's platform terms.

How much third-party text the distillate carries was measured on 2026-10-24
with the framework's scripts/third_party_overlap.py (a run of n words that
occurs in third-party text and never in the agent's own sections; a floor,
not a full count): 371 of 12,628 patterns share a 12-word run (555 at 8
words, 148 at 20), none before July 2026; 46 of 82 weekly documents in
reports/analysis/ do at 12 words (56 at 8); 4 of 12 unique snapshot
reasoning.md files do; snapshot skills do not. The Hugging Face
`patterns.jsonl` projection is the same pattern text as knowledge.json.

